    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 231131 CCA\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n331 AM PDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Isolated shower chances and breezy conditions stick around for a \n  few more days as a trough lingers in the region.\n\n* Drier and calmer conditions resume next week with seasonable\n  temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Thursday.\n\nThe shortwave that spurred all of the showers and storms today has \nlifted northeast, allowing drier conditions to settle in. A \nsecondary shortwave is diving south on the backside of the parent \ntrough, keeping the trough overhead today and transforming it into a \nclosed low. Cold air aloft, residual moisture, and some daytime \nsolar heating should allow some isolated instability showers (10-30% \nchances) to develop today, mainly across the northern half of the \nCWA. Most of the region stays dry though, with below normal \ntemperatures and just some breezy winds in our northwestern zones. \nThe low slowly drift east tomorrow, leaving 10-30% PoPs across \neastern Mohave County. Farther west, dry conditions are expected \nwith gusty north winds of 20-35 mph. \n\nDry conditions anticipated areawide Sunday - Thursday as the low \nfinally exits and a quasi-zonal pattern sets up. Some breezy \nconditions are possible in the southern Great Basin early in the \nweek as a shortwave moves through the PacNW, but otherwise winds \nremain light. Temperatures rebound to seasonable values and hold \nfairly steady throughout the week.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Light \nwinds last through the day and into the night with strong winds \narriving late Friday night. Expect mostly variable winds through the \nmorning before becoming more northeast into the late morning. Winds \nwill turn northwest into the night but remain light. Stronger, north-\nnorthwesterly winds arrive into the late night and last beyond the \nend of the TAF period. Gusts around 25 kts are expected with \ninfrequent gusts approaching 30 kts possible. Mostly clear skies \nlast through the TAF period. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Expect mostly light \nwinds across the region for much of the day. KDAG looks to see \nslightly more moderate winds this morning, but these winds will \nlighten into the afternoon. Stronger north and northwest winds and \ngusts arrive into the evening (for KBIH) and overnight for all but \nKDAG which looks to stay sheltered from these winds. Gusts will \nrange from 20 to 30 kts across much of the region. These winds will \nbeing to reduce further into Saturday morning. Mostly clear skies \nlast through the TAF period. \n\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Woods\nAVIATION...Murdock\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
